<rect x="520" y="40" width="160" height="56" rx="6" fill="rgba(45,49,66,0.05)" stroke="#4f5d75"/><text x="600" y="72">Supabase Auth</text>
<rect x="520" y="140" width="160" height="56" rx="6" fill="rgba(45,49,66,0.05)" stroke="#4f5d75"/><text x="600" y="172">Postgres + RLS</text>
<rect x="520" y="260" width="160" height="56" rx="6" fill="rgba(45,49,66,0.03)" stroke="rgba(45,49,66,0.3)"/><text x="600" y="292">Resend</text>
<rect x="760" y="260" width="140" height="56" rx="6" fill="rgba(45,49,66,0.03)" stroke="rgba(45,49,66,0.3)"/><text x="830" y="292">Stripe</text>
</g>
<line x1="30" y1="384" x2="890" y2="384" stroke="rgba(45,49,66,0.10)" stroke-width="0.8"/>
<text x="30" y="404" fill="#4f5d75" font-size="8" font-family="'Geist Mono', monospace" letter-spacing="0.14em">LEGEND  SOLID = REQUEST   DASHED = SCHEDULED   GREY = EXTERNAL   STRIPE WEBHOOK RETURNS TO HANDLERS</text>
</svg>
<figcaption>Next.js route handlers on Vercel are the only way in. Stripe also calls back <code>POST /api/v1/billing/webhook</code> (not in the OpenAPI spec).</figcaption>
</figure>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th><th>Touches</th><th>Why it matters for QA</th></tr>
          <tr><td><code>middleware.ts</code></td><td>refreshes the Supabase session on page requests; redirects protected UI paths to <code>/login</code></td><td>Supabase Auth</td><td>does not gate <code>/api/v1</code>: API auth is in the handler</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>withApiHandler</code></td><td>auth posture, capability check, error envelope, request id</td><td>all routes</td><td>a posture mismatch shows as 401 or 403, never a silent pass; a snapshot test pins every route's posture</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Idempotency middleware</td><td><code>Idempotency-Key</code> replay guard (8-128 chars, per user and endpoint)</td><td><code>idempotency_keys</code></td><td>required on <code>POST /tests</code>, <code>/runs</code>, <code>/test-plans/{id}/tests</code>, billing checkout; same key with a different body returns 409</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Postgres RPCs and RLS</td><td>authorization and atomic business rules</td><td>all tables</td><td>cross-workspace access answers 404, not 403, on several routes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Vercel Cron</td><td>calls <code>/admin/send-digest</code> daily at 08:00 (<code>vercel.json</code>)</td><td>Resend, notifications</td><td>manual retry via POST with the system secret</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p><strong>Error envelope:</strong> every failure is <code>{"error": {"code", "message", "details?", "request_id?"}}</code>. Branch on <code>code</code> (<code>validation_failed</code>, <code>unauthorized</code>, <code>forbidden</code>, <code>not_found</code>, <code>conflict</code>, <code>idempotency_key_required</code>, <code>rate_limited</code> plus the domain codes above), never on <code>message</code>.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="integrations" data-sources="route:app/api/v1/billing/webhook/route.ts,route:lib/billing/stripe.ts,route:lib/mail/resend-client.ts,route:vercel.json,openapi:Imports,openapi:Auth" data-updated="2026-10-05">
        <h2>External integrations at the API boundary</h2>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Service</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Direction</th><th>Failure mode (user-visible)</th><th>Journeys affected</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Stripe</td><td><code>POST /workspaces/{id}/billing/checkout</code></td><td>outbound sync</td><td>503 when Stripe keys are unset; 409 if a session is already open</td><td><code>journey-upgrade-billing</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stripe</td><td><code>POST /billing/webhook</code></td><td>inbound async, signature-verified</td><td>missed event leaves the workspace on Community after payment; unknown session answers 5xx so Stripe retries</td><td><code>journey-upgrade-billing</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Resend</td><td>cron or manual <code>POST /admin/send-digest</code>; auth emails</td><td>outbound async</td><td>digest silently skipped without <code>RESEND_API_KEY</code> (optional env); sign-up code and magic link rely on Supabase mail</td><td>notifications, <code>journey-headless-auth</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Supabase Auth</td><td>all <code>/auth/*</code>, every Bearer or cookie call</td><td>outbound sync</td><td>magic link answers 502 when the mail provider fails; 429 on rate-limited sign-up and magic link</td><td>all</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jira Cloud</td><td><code>POST /imports</code></td><td>outbound async job</td><td>returns 202 with a job id; errors and counts appear on <code>GET /imports/{id}</code>; one active import per project (409)</td><td>stories and criteria setup</td></tr>
        </table>
      </section>
      <section id="cross-references" data-sources="openapi:*,route:api/schemas/" data-updated="2026-10-05">
        <h2>Cross-references</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Entities, state machines and triggers: <code>bun run context:map business-data-context</code> (ids cited above as <code>entity-*</code> and <code>state-*</code>).</li>
          <li>Journeys, personas and the feature catalog: <code>bun run context:map business-e2e-context</code> (ids cited above as <code>journey-*</code>).</li>
          <li>Full endpoint contracts: OpenAPI at <code>https://staging-upexbunkai.vercel.app/api/openapi</code>; Scalar docs at <code>/api/docs</code> on the same host.</li>
          <li>Typed facades for tests: <code>api/schemas/auth.types.ts</code> and <code>atc.types.ts</code> (<code>bun run api:sync</code> regenerates the base types). Only auth and ATC are wired into KATA components today.</li>
          <li>Stack, environments and secrets: <code>bun run context:map infra-context</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section id="discovery-gaps" data-sources="openapi:*" data-updated="2026-10-05">
        <h2>Discovery gaps</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The May 2026 legacy map described 40 endpoints and an unversioned auth story; this map was rebuilt from the live spec (102 operations) and the target repo at <code>36198b9d</code>. Anything the legacy file said that is not repeated here was not re-verified.</li>
          <li><code>POST /api/v1/billing/webhook</code> and <code>GET/OPTIONS /api/openapi</code> exist in code but not in the OpenAPI spec.</li>
          <li>Rate limiting: the error code <code>rate_limited</code> and 429 responses exist on sign-up and magic link, but I could not find an app-level limiter in <code>lib/api/</code>; it is probably Supabase Auth throttling. Not measured.</li>
          <li>Role-by-role access (viewer, member, admin, owner) is enforced in RLS policies that I did not read route by route; the tier table covers capabilities, not roles.</li>
          <li>Per-route Idempotency-Key requirement was confirmed on four routes by code search; other write routes may accept the header without requiring it.</li>
          <li><code>business-e2e-context</code> ids were aligned to its generated map on 2026-10-05; <code>business-data-context</code> was still a placeholder then, so its cited <code>entity-*</code> and <code>state-*</code> ids are planned slugs to re-check.</li>
          <li>Env values (Stripe price id, Resend sender, Supabase project) were read by name only; no secrets were opened.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
